68334884868,"version":"3.49.0"},"description":"A new health policy brief from Health Affairs with support from the Robert Wood Johnson Foundation examines the potential health impacts of urban gentrification on original (or legacy) neighborhood residents.","reference-count":0,"publisher":"Health Affairs Publishing, LLC","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2020,8,17]]},"DOI":"10.1377\/forefront.20200817.282985","type":"dataset","created":{"date-parts":[[2022,3,10]],"date-time":"2022-03-10T14:58:33Z","timestamp":1646924313000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Health Policy Brief:  Gentrification And The Health Of Legacy Residents"],"prefix":"10.1377","member":"102","container-title":["Forefront Group"],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2022,3,10]],"date-time":"2022-03-10T15:03:10Z","timestamp":1646924590000},"score":26.281094,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"http:\/\/www.healthaffairs.org\/do\/10.1377\/forefront.20200817.282985\/full\/"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2020,8,17]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1377\/forefront.20200817.282985","published":{"date-parts":[[2020,8,17]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,11,14]],"date-time":"2026-11-14T09:46:35Z","timestamp":1794649595569,"version":"4.9.1"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"Oxford University Press","isbn-type":[{"value":"9780199542550","type":"print"},{"value":"9780191917738","type":"electronic"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2010,7,15]]},"abstract":"<p>The new Station 5, Integrative Clinical Assessment involves two 10-minute encounters, each known as a \u2018Brief Clinical Consultation\u2019. Following an introductory referral, the candidate has 8 minutes to undertake a focused history and examination to solve a clinical problem, answer any questions the patient may have and explain their investigation and\/or treatment plan to the patient. The remaining 2 minutes are spent with the examiners, to relate the relevant physical findings and differential diagnosis. Remember, you are not expected to take a complete history or conduct a complete and thorough examination, as you would in the other stations. Candidates should be prepared to encounter scenarios relating to: 1. Old Station 5 cases, i.e. skin, eye, locomotor, and endocrine systems. 2. Other stations of the examination (stations 1 and 3). 3. Medical problems encountered in everyday practice, i.e. chest pain, hypotension, jaundice, and deterioration in renal function. In principle, this station can include any possible inpatient and outpatient medical scenario, and therefore providing a comprehensive selection of cases will never be feasible. Some patients may not display a wealth of clinical signs, and this often occurs in everyday practice. The candidate should understand the key principles, and develop the art of integrative clinical assessment. This will ensure success in any clinical scenario provided. This integrated approach is a test of higher clinical reasoning and professionalism, rather than a simple test of clinical skills\u2014 this should be kept in mind when preparing for this station. The compilation of 20 cases in this section is designed to achieve this, and encourages the candidate to adopt a uniform style, and a thoughtful approach and strategy in tackling this station. \u2022 Explanatory referrals are provided in the 5 minute interval before the station. \u2022 Read these carefully, and identify the clinical problem(s). \u2022 Develop a differential diagnosis based on the limited information available, even before seeing the patient. \u2022 A preliminary differential diagnosis will initially help guide the focused history. \u2022 The history and examination should not be seen as separate components, where the history is followed by the examination. \u2022 Instead, both history and examination should be integrated.<\/p>","DOI":"10.1093\/oso\/9780199542550.003.0012","type":"book-chapter","created":{"date-parts":[[2020,11,10]],"date-time":"2020-11-10T20:34:29Z","timestamp":1605040469000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Brief Clinical Consultations: General Approach to Brief Clinical Consultations"],"prefix":"10.1093","author":[{"given":"Gautam","family":"Mehta","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Bilal","family":"Iqbal","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"286","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2020,11,12]]},"container-title":["Clinical Medicine for the MRCP PACES"],"original-title":["Brief Clinical Consultations: General Approach to Brief Clinical Consultations"],"language":"en","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2022,8,2]],"date-time":"2022-08-02T16:52:40Z","timestamp":1659459160000},"score":25.736084,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/academic.oup.com\/book\/40276\/chapter\/346757322"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2010,7,15]]},"ISBN":["9780199542550","9780191917738"],"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1093\/oso\/9780199542550.003.0012","published":{"date-parts":[[2010,7,15]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,20]],"date-time":"2026-10-20T09:51:51Z","timestamp":1792489911210,"version":"4.5.0"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"Wiley","issue":"5","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2016,4,13]],"date-time":"2016-04-13T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1460505600000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/termsAndConditions#vor"}],"content-domain":{"domain":["asmepublications.onlinelibrary.wiley.com"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"short-container-title":["Medical Education"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2016,5]]},"DOI":"10.1111\/medu.13047","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2016,4,13]],"date-time":"2016-04-13T06:49:40Z","timestamp":1460530180000},"page":"573-574","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":10,"title":["The communal consultation: video\u2010recorded student consultations"],"prefix":"10.1111","volume":"50","author":[{"given":"Michael","family":"Botelho","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"311","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2016,4,13]]},"container-title":["Medical Education"],"language":"en","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/api.wiley.com\/onlinelibrary\/tdm\/v1\/articles\/10.1111%2Fmedu.13047","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/asmepublications.onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/doi\/pdf\/10.1111\/medu.13047","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2025,11,4]],"date-time":"2025-11-04T18:24:53Z","timestamp":1762280693000},"score":21.548101,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/asmepublications.onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/doi\/10.1111\/medu.13047"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2016,4,13]]},"references-count":0,"journal-issue":{"issue":"5","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2016,5]]}},"alternative-id":["10.1111\/medu.13047"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1111\/medu.13047","archive":["Portico"],"ISSN":["0308-0110","1365-2923"],"issn-type":[{"value":"0308-0110","type":"print"},{"value":"1365-2923","type":"electronic"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2016,4,13]]},"assertion":[{"value":"2016-04-13","order":3,"name":"published","label":"Published","group":{"name":"publication_history","label":"Publication History"}}]},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,13]],"date-time":"2026-08-13T12:36:49Z","timestamp":1786624609814,"version":"build-2736575974"},"posted":{"date-parts":[[2016]]},"group-title":"SSRN","reference-count":43,"publisher":"Elsevier BV","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"abstract":"<jats:p>This article concerns the important issues of access to justice and practical lawyering skills. Clients are representing themselves in family law matters in ever increasing numbers.  Courts, bar groups, nonprofits and law schools have responded by offering \u201cbrief advice\u201d clinics.  How well these clinics operate can significantly influence the public\u2019s access to justice. This article analyses actual consultations in a brief advice clinic relying upon transcriptions of recordings and using conversation analysis techniques. This analysis demonstrates that the matters brought to the clinic are not \u201csimple\u201d ones where legal representation is not needed. These clients are facing serious problems from domestic violence, to abandonment, to denial of visitation, and they have many questions and strong feelings about their circumstances. Fortunately, experienced attorneys who specialize in family law are able to analyze these matters and provide strategic, personalized counseling and relevant information. Unfortunately, these lawyers often rush to provide information they believe will be helpful before they fully understand the client\u2019s situation and goals. These volunteer attorneys are motivated to share all they know, and sometimes flood these clients with information.  The clients, in turn, strive to share their stories and rationales, even when the lawyers would prefer to review their papers and ask them yes\/no questions. The result is that both attorneys and clients may feel they are drinking from a fire hose. The article carefully analyzes the successes and failures in these consultations and concludes by outlining best practices for interviewing and counseling in a brief advice clinic.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.2139\/ssrn.2729008","type":"posted-content","created":{"date-parts":[[2016,2,10]],"date-time":"2016-02-10T20:57:31Z","timestamp":1455137851000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Drinking from a Firehose:  Conversation Analysis of Consultations in a Brief Advice Clinic"],"prefix":"10.2139","author":[{"given":"Linda","family":"Smith","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"78","reference":[{"key":"ref1","author":"Ms","journal-title":"Attorney2 Yeah something like that, like two fifty"},{"key":"ref2","author":"Ms","journal-title":"to modify you have to allege that there has been material change of circumstances--something has really changed (hmhm) since your divorce and that this supervised part should be taken off. So I'm not sure whether the judge will let you do that by a motion or not"},{"key":"ref3","journal-title":"Vic I've never had supervised visits, ever (Right) since we've been divorced, she's just dropped him off"},{"key":"ref4","author":"Ms","journal-title":"Attorney 1 And and that's certainly, and I think that's how you can probably get in"},{"key":"ref5","author":"Ms","journal-title":"Attorney 2 [Well and what's in] the divorce decree"},{"key":"ref6","author":"Ms","journal-title":"Attorney 1 [Supervised] visits. Vic Supervised visits"},{"key":"ref7","author":"Ms","journal-title":"Attorney 2 Ok Ms. Attorney 1 But he's saying he"},{"key":"ref8","author":"Vic"},{"key":"ref9","author":"Ms","journal-title":"Attorney 1 got them Vic I've never had them"},{"key":"ref10","author":"Ms","journal-title":"Attorney1 So this is a motion to enforce visitation \"and by the way judge, let's drop the supervised part"},{"key":"ref11","journal-title":"Girlfriend So maybe if this doesn't work, (yes yes) and the judge says go back (yes) and [then maybe look into it"},{"key":"ref12","author":"Ms","journal-title":"Attorney 1 [Yes I would agree with that"},{"key":"ref13","author":"Vic","journal-title":"Cause she had an attorney, then they just all of a sudden they just dropped it. We're sittin' there, and she didn't show up, but she didn't even call the court or nothing. Before I got there I literally called his office and ask him what happened. (MmHm) And she's just like well what's going to happen, and she's not comin' and so, therefore I thought I would win"},{"key":"ref14","author":"Ms","journal-title":"Attorney 1 [Yes, she's] a commissioner"},{"key":"ref15","journal-title":"Vic So she didn't get all the facts in, and I'm like, I gave her everything pretty much. So I just wanted to know, so you think I should just"},{"key":"ref16","author":"Ms","journal-title":"Attorney 1 I think you should run with it. Vic Run with it?"},{"key":"ref17","author":"Ms","journal-title":"Attorney 1 Yeah, just understand that it's possible that the judge could say at some point, you know"},{"key":"ref18","journal-title":"And that means, you know when you get day care for your kid, you pay half of course. But it doesn't say you pay half of their private school tuition. That's what we're looking for now to see if there's a clause that says that"},{"key":"ref19","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","author":"Attorney2","DOI":"10.6027\/anp2018-778"},{"key":"ref20","journal-title":"Attorney1 And then there's life insurance, debts, see that's what, this doesn't seem to me like the type of document that's detailed enough to get into private schools"},{"key":"ref21","journal-title":"Girlfriend So how would he go about getting that?"},{"key":"ref22","journal-title":"Attorney1 I'd go to ORS if they're taking it and take your thing (OK) and say hey it's not in here"},{"key":"ref23","journal-title":"Attorney1 You do a motion in court just like you did here and say you shouldn't be responsible for private school when I didn't agree to be in my decree"},{"key":"ref24","journal-title":"But it's still a Montessori school I guess. I don't know if that's like. Attorney1 Oh, so it is kind of like a daycare? Girlfriend Well it's still private, it's still a private institution"},{"key":"ref25","journal-title":"Attorney2 So she's not dropping him off at someone's house to play with blocks all day. It's like structured educational environment"},{"key":"ref26","journal-title":"Attorney1 I think it's not covered in your divorce decree"},{"key":"ref27","journal-title":"Attorney2 Yeah it doesn't sound like it"},{"key":"ref28","journal-title":"Attorney1 So I don't think you should have to pay for it. (Okay) Well I think we've pretty much covered it. Does it make sense? Vic Yes"},{"key":"ref29","article-title":"They forget there is just one child (referring to \"they\" and \"kids\") and do not interview about the child's age or explore whether this expense could be childcare for a pre-school child. Despite Vic's statement that \"it's like $900 a month\" the attorneys do not explore what is $900 a month (his total support? the total cost of the school? his share of the school expense?) or explore whether this cost is reasonable for child care","journal-title":"private school\") and attempt to answer his legal question by looking through the decree and without interviewing him about the situation"},{"key":"ref30","journal-title":"Vic Just to follow up? Ms. Attorney 1"},{"key":"ref31","author":"Ms","journal-title":"Attorney2 [Yeah] and the bottom line is you want to see your kids right?"},{"key":"ref32","journal-title":"Vic [Yeah I mean it's been four months"},{"key":"ref33","author":"Ms","journal-title":"Girlfriend He you know offered to be flexible whatever she wanted. He was totally an open book. He was like come to our house, see where we live, see our environment, meet my friends, meet whatever you want, like I'll be willing to do and she's justVic Yeah"},{"key":"ref34","journal-title":"Attorney2 Yeah, she's obviously not very happy with you. Client 1 She wasn't happy"},{"key":"ref35","journal-title":"Attorney1 What you do is you just put it in that pink box (ok) up there when you're done. And we're actually going to head back with another group (ok) right here. 'Cause I think there's room at the table. (ok) So I"},{"key":"ref36","journal-title":"Vic Thank you I'mMs. Attorney 1 I'm really"},{"key":"ref37","author":"Ms","journal-title":"Attorney 2 [And you guys know] when we're here, right? Vic Just every Wednesday, right? Ms. Attorney 2 Every other"},{"key":"ref38","author":"Vic"},{"key":"ref39","author":"Ms","journal-title":"Attorney 2 It's the first and third Wednesdays, right? Ms. Attorney 1 Yes. (ok) Hopefully you can"},{"key":"ref40","author":"Vic","journal-title":"Yeah so I'll come back after my court"},{"key":"ref41","author":"Ms","journal-title":"Attorney 1 Well you're definitely doing the right stuff. Ms. Attorney 2 Yeah. Vic I'll let you know what happens"},{"key":"ref42","author":"Ms","journal-title":"Attorney 1 Alright and you've got a good judge. She's really nice. Girlfriend She seems like it"},{"key":"ref43","author":"Ms","journal-title":"She's smart. Girlfriend We've been in there a couple of times. Vic Yeah, she's kind of"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,13]],"date-time":"2026-08-13T12:11:37Z","timestamp":1786623097000},"score":20.385458,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/www.ssrn.com\/abstract=2729008"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2016]]},"references-count":43,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.2139\/ssrn.2729008","published":{"date-parts":[[2016]]},"subtype":"preprint"}],"items-per-page":5,"query":{"start-index":0,"search-terms":null}}}